<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Output compliance diagnostics</title><style>body{max-width:1260px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px 80px;background:#f8fafc;color:#193047;font:17px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}h1{font-size:2.35rem;line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2.3rem;line-height:1.3}a{color:#087f8c}img{max-width:100%;height:auto;background:white;border-radius:10px}table{display:block;overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.86rem;margin:20px 0}th,td{border-bottom:1px solid #d5dfe9;padding:9px 11px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#e6eef5}code{font-size:.85em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{overflow:auto;background:#e6eef5;padding:16px}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-bottom:1px solid #d5dfe9;padding-bottom:16px;font-size:.9rem}p{max-width:100ch}</style></head><body><nav><a href="index.html">Overall comparison</a><a href="functions.html">Functions and load</a><a href="three_model_reference.html">Original three-model reference</a><a href="https://github.com/etsabary/jev-1.14-comparison-benchmark">Repository and evidence</a></nav><main><h1 id="output-compliance-diagnostics">Output compliance diagnostics</h1>
<p>Haiku 5.5, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash and Phi-4 had substantial difficulty returning only a numeric decision within the 16-token output limit. Their saved runs remain public, but they are excluded from the <a href="index.html">main benchmark</a>, function tables and comparative charts.</p>
<p>The author requested this separation after reviewing the outputs. The reporting rule excludes a model when at least <strong>5% of the 1,136 planned first attempts</strong> fail the output contract. This is a post-hoc operational cutoff, not a preregistered rule or a statistical significance test. HTTP errors, connection failures, body-read timeouts and upstream error envelopes are counted separately and do not trigger this format exclusion. Lower levels of format failure remain unsuccessful first attempts in the main results.</p>
<p>All models were asked to return only option ID 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5, with reasoning disabled and <code>max_tokens=16</code>. No malformed answer was retried. A valid but wrong choice was not retried either. Permitted API recovery attempts and their charges remain separate from the primary first-attempt scores.</p>
<h2 id="three-unranked-runs">Three unranked runs</h2>
<p>The strict full-bank figures below describe success under the tested output contract. They are diagnostic results, not entries in the main accuracy ranking. Accuracy among usable answers is conditional on which questions a model answered directly; it cannot be extrapolated to the unanswered questions.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Unranked diagnostic</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Usable / 1,136</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Model-output failures</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Provider failures</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Correct among usable</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Strict full-bank result</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Median</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Known run cost</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Phi-4 14B</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">807</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">327</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">2</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">428/807 (53.0%)</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">428/1,136 (37.7%)</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">365 ms</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">$0.02329726</td>
